This project is derived from Pretendo Network (https://github.com/PretendoNetwork),
an open-source reimplementation of Nintendo's discontinued Wii U/3DS online
services. It reimplements the Wii U NEX (matchmaking/ranking) protocol for
FAST Racing NEO on top of Pretendo Network's open-source Go libraries:

  - nex-go               https://github.com/PretendoNetwork/nex-go
  - nex-protocols-go      https://github.com/PretendoNetwork/nex-protocols-go
  - nex-protocols-common-go
                          https://github.com/PretendoNetwork/nex-protocols-common-go
  - plogger-go            https://github.com/PretendoNetwork/plogger-go

All are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.

`third_party/nex-protocols-common-go-trace` is a locally modified fork of
`nex-protocols-common-go`: it adds per-protocol call tracking/logging
(`tracking/log_*.go` files) alongside the upstream matchmaking, matchmake
extension, and ranking handlers. Everything else in that tree is
unmodified upstream code. This notice serves as the AGPL-3.0 Section 5
statement that the file has been changed and carries a relevant date.

The guest account credential in globals/accounts.go ("guest" /
"MMQea3n!fsik") is not a Protarium secret — it's the well-known default
guest login built into the Quazal/NEX middleware itself, used by some
titles before a real account login.

No proprietary Nintendo, Shin'en Multimedia, or other third-party game
code or assets are included in this repository.
